<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;ZOOBLES!&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Zoobles! is a popular animated television series originating from Brazil, known for promoting environmental awareness and cultural exchange."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRAZIL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Brazil is a country in South America where Zoobles! originated and where the show's roots can be traced back to the vibrant cultural landscape."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARLOS ALBERTO DOS SANTOS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carlos Alberto dos Santos is a renowned Brazilian animator and director who first conceived the concept of Zoobles! in the early 2000s."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RIO DE JANEIRO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rio de Janeiro is the city where Carlos Alberto dos Santos is from and drew inspiration for Zoobles! from the country's rich folklore and biodiversity."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ESTÚDIO DE ANIMAÇÃO BRASILEIRA (EAB)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Estúdio de Animação Brasileira (EAB) is a Brazilian animation studio founded by Carlos Alberto dos Santos to develop the concept of Zoobles! into a full-fledged television series."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRAZILIAN MINISTRY OF CULTURE AND EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Brazilian Ministry of Culture and Education partnered with EAB to provide funding and resources for the development of Zoobles! as a tool for promoting Brazilian culture and values."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JOURNAL OF LATIN AMERICAN MEDIA STUDIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Journal of Latin American Media Studies published a study in 2010 that found Zoobles! to be instrumental in promoting cultural exchange and understanding between Brazil and other countries."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRAZILIAN JOURNAL OF EDUCATION AND RESEARCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Brazilian Journal of Education and Research published a study in 2015 that found Zoobles! to be an effective tool for teaching environmental education and promoting sustainability among children."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SAMG ANIMATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SamG Animation is a Seoul-based production company that produced Zoobles! and has a strong presence in South Korea."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEOUL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Seoul is the city where SamG Animation is based and where the South Korean connection to Zoobles! is rooted."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOUTH KOREA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"South Korea is a country in East Asia that has become a hub for innovative animation and entertainment and is the origin of Zoobles!' production company, SamG Animation."&lt;SEP&gt;"South Korea is the origin of the voice actors and the cultural inspiration for the show."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHIKO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chiko is a character name inspired by Korean culture, used in the show."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chiko is a character name used in Zoobles!, reflecting South Korean cultural values and sensibilities."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JIKO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Jiko is another character name inspired by Korean culture, used in the show."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jiko is another character name used in Zoobles!, further emphasizing the show's South Korean origins."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OLIVEIRA, M.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mariana Oliveira is the author of a study published in 2010 that found Zoobles! to be instrumental in promoting cultural exchange and understanding between Brazil and other countries."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SILVA, J.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"João Silva is the author of a study published in 2015 that found Zoobles! to be an effective tool for teaching environmental education and promoting sustainability among children."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DOS SANTOS, C. A.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carlos Alberto dos Santos is the founder of Estúdio de Animação Brasileira (EAB) and the creator of Zoobles!"</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SAMG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SamG is a Seoul-based production company that produced Zoobles! and has a strong presence in South Korea."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VOICE CAST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The voice cast includes talented South Korean voice actors who contribute to the show's cultural authenticity."&lt;SEP&gt;"The voice cast of Zoobles! includes talented South Korean voice actors who have contributed to the show's success."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JAPANESE ANIMATION INDUSTRY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Japanese animation industry is mentioned as a competitor to South Korea's animation industry."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHINESE ANIMATION INDUSTRY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Chinese animation industry is mentioned as a competitor to South Korea's animation industry."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VISIONARY ANIMATORS AND PRODUCERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A small group of visionary animators and producers in Seoul were determined to make a mark on the global stage."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KOREAN CULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Korean culture refers to the cultural aspects and traditions of Korea, including names, voice actors, and animation styles."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOUTH KOREAN VOICE ACTORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"South Korean voice actors are talented performers who contribute to the show's voice cast, many of whom have worked on other successful projects."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRODUCTION TEAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The production team is responsible for the creation and development of the show, incorporating elements of South Korean culture and creativity."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANIMATION STYLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The animation style of the show reflects South Korean artistic techniques and aesthetics, contributing to its cultural identity."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUCCESSFUL ANIMATED SERIES AND FILMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Successful animated series and films are mentioned as works by South Korean voice actors, indicating their talent and industry success."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANIMATED SERIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Animated series are part of the broader context of successful works by South Korean voice actors."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FILMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Films are part of the broader context of successful works by South Korean voice actors."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0499</data>
    </node>
